{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And she had an Egyptian maidservant.</b> And not he — our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: she was melog-property (a wife's personal belongings), and he was not entitled to sell her." "<b>And her name was Hagar.</b> Pharaoh's household gave her to her, and therefore she was called <b>Hagar</b> — הא אגריך, that is: הגר — reward (s'khar) for your modesty."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:12:39.762100769Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}